    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 455 of 2011",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S983          Revised 5/6/2025\n\nSPONSOR: ROLISON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 455 of the laws of 2011 amending the environ-\nmental conservation law relating to authorizing angling by a single\nindividual with up to three lines in freshwater, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nEliminates the expiration date and extends the date to two years from\nexpiration, with provisions of law authorizing an individual to fish\nwith up to 3 lines in freshwater.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nlegislation amends chapter 455 of the laws of 2011, amending the envi-\nronmental conservation law relating to authorizing angling by a single\nindividual with up to three lines in freshwater, to extend the\nprovisions thereof by two years.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe original legislation (Chapter 455, L. 2011) expires on December 31,\n2025. This bill will extend the legislation to December 31, 2027.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS5376 of 2023: Signed Chapter 419\n\nS2044 of 2021: Signed Chapter 281\n\nS2461 of 2019: Signed Chapter 394\n\nS6239 of 2017: Signed Chapter 207\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
